  "body": "Revising the 2026-05-25T21:00 dispositions on the three queued gap-proposals after PO directive 2026-05-25 evening pushed back on the strict-reading value-#4 interpretation. **CA-010 filed** formalizing the 'designated reference user' pattern (generalizing the existing canonical-reference-file practice) and designating Thingalog as the first reference user of catdef. With that designation in place, Thingalog gap-proposals qualify as cross-implementer demand for value-#4 promotion gating without requiring a second unrelated implementer to converge on the same shape. Pipeline discipline (no backdoor amendments; gap-proposals flow through normal strategist-triage-then-Director-ratification) is preserved unchanged. **Revised dispositions:** **Gap 3 (primary-index Phase 2)** — PROMOTE to v1.5 lead. Drop the 'second non-Thingalog implementer' gate. Thingalog Phase 1 x.primary_index shipping (slice 11.1) constitutes the empirical reference shape; multiple Thingalog tenants with different primary-index modes (magazine-archive Documents-first, PXMemories People-first, calendar Events-first) constitute sufficient demand surface for canonical promotion under CA-010. Promotion can begin as soon as the v1.5 cycle is triggered. **Gap 2 (recursive table fields / rich-Value internal structure)** — PROMOTE to v1.5 cycle inclusion; design as part of the value-shape bundle (with item-level-polymorphism + CA-007 Table-cell-translatability). Drop the 'second-implementer demonstration' gate. The universal-renderer doctrine motivation + multiple Thingalog tenant use cases (PXMemories Person values, Bill's-Wedding Place values, magazine-archive Article values) qualify as sufficient demand surface under CA-010. Coordinated-design requirement (with item-level-polymorphism + CA-007) STANDS — value-shape questions need one coherent answer, not three independent ones. **Gap 1 (audio attachment field type)** — DEFER, but on revised grounds. NOT 'insufficient cross-implementer demand' (CA-010 makes that moot for Thingalog-driven gaps). The hold is now on **insufficient empirical surface** — PXMemories has not shipped, so there is no actual audio shape to design canonical against. Promotion gate revised: when PXMemories ships with audio-attachment use cases, Gap 1 enters v1.5 (or v1.6, depending on cycle timing). This is a practical-design constraint, not a values-policing one. **Updated v1.5 work pickup list:** Gaps 2 and 3 promoted from 'deferred pending second implementer' to 'queued for v1.5 cycle.' Gap 1 promoted from 'deferred indefinitely' to 'deferred pending PXMemories ship.' Full revised list in body_ref. **Original 21:00 memo stays as institutional record of the first read.** It captured the strict-value-#4 interpretation accurately. This revision records the update after CA-010 formalized the reference-user pattern. Both artifacts preserved; no rewriting.",
  "body_ref": "2026-05-25-2200--catdef-strategist--thingalog-strategist--revised-dispositions-per-CA-010-reference-user-designation.body.md",

